---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Docs — Ruvio" description="Reference layout trial.">
  <main><div class="wrap docs">
    <aside class="side">
      <h4>Get started</h4><a href="#">Install</a><a class="on" href="#">Run a node</a><a href="#">Connect a client</a>
      <h4>Reference</h4><a href="#">Commands</a><a href="#">Configuration</a><a href="#">Durability</a><a href="#">Replication</a>
      <h4>Operate</h4><a href="#">Metrics</a><a href="#">Backups</a>
    </aside>
    <article class="doc">
      <p class="kicker">Get started</p>
      <h1>Run a node</h1>
      <p>A default server listens on <code>127.0.0.1:6379</code>. The operator UI is a second process on port 8080.</p>
      <h2>With Docker</h2>
      <pre>docker run --rm -p 6379:6379 salihcantekin/ruvio:latest</pre>
      <div class="callout"><b>Durability.</b> Pick <code>memory</code>, <code>snapshot</code>, <code>everysec</code> or <code>always</code> at startup. The page this layout would carry is the real Durability reference.</div>
      <h2>Check it works</h2>
      <pre>redis-cli PING
# PONG</pre>
      <div class="pager"><a href="#">← Install</a><a href="#">Connect a client →</a></div>
    </article>
  </div></main>
</Base>
